Z||000016||theogre||04-18-2000||08:16 PM||||The first one in the thread bites. The one in the yellow car is better but I don't really like it either.<P>Light systems that don't use DOT legal <I>head lamps</I> are illegal in all 50 states. Any modification of headlight systems is illegal in some states. fog/driving/orwhatever they are ain't DOT head lights.<P>Canada has similar restrictions, some vary by province.<P>Then there's the insurance, civil and posible criminal penalties if your in an accident that can be blaimed on a modifoed system, especially if it doesn't use DOT approved lamps, and use them as required. For example using only the high/low lamps out of the quad lamp setup doesn't meet DOT regs.<P>As I rememebre Toms original set is using a DOT lamp set, and it looks like it could have been stock. So even where any modification is illegal it would likely not be bothered.<P>There is a smaller format dual lamp set that could be adapted. That would lower the profile. might leave room for a driving light as well. (The smaller format is in between the ones we have stock and the small rectangle lamps used in quads.) You might could even get room for an extra turn signal lamp for better visibilty by other traffic in crappy weather.||||reg||1
